D3D12: the pipeline library's expected paths draw no debug-layer warning; a refused cache says why.

DeviceD3D12 already denies CREATEPIPELINELIBRARY_INVALIDLIBRARYBLOB [962], since PipelineCacheD3D12
answers a blob that is no library with "OUT_OF_DATE". A blob from another driver or adapter takes
the same path but draws its own WARNING: [963] DRIVERVERSIONMISMATCH ("intended for a different
driver version") and [964] ADAPTERVERSIONMISMATCH, so a cache saved before a driver update warns at
the next start, in debug runs only. PipelineD3D12 looks every pipeline up with LoadPipeline /
LoadComputePipeline before creating and storing it, and each miss draws [971]
LOADPIPELINE_NAMENOTFOUND ("This library does not have a pipeline stored with name ..."): every
first creation, so every changed shader in a debug run. The three join the deny list.

"OUT_OF_DATE" itself said nothing of the cause, which CreatePipelineLibrary's result names
(D3D12_ERROR_DRIVER_VERSION_MISMATCH, D3D12_ERROR_ADAPTER_NOT_FOUND): PipelineCacheD3D12 now reports
it as an INFO, in every build ("Pipeline cache data refused: made by another driver version
(result = 0x887E0002)"), and still returns "OUT_OF_DATE".

Measured on v191, Agility 1.620, NVIDIA (2026-11-08): a miss gave [971]; one byte flipped at offsets
16-23 of a real serialization gave [963], at 28-59 [964], at 0-15 and 24-27 the denied [962], each
with "OUT_OF_DATE". Main a20efc8f has the same code.

diff --git a/Source/D3D12/DeviceD3D12.hpp b/Source/D3D12/DeviceD3D12.hpp
index 7446e603..6dbb82e4 100644
--- a/Source/D3D12/DeviceD3D12.hpp
+++ b/Source/D3D12/DeviceD3D12.hpp
@@ -636,6 +636,11 @@ Result DeviceD3D12::Create(const DeviceCreationDesc& desc, const DeviceCreationD
                 D3D12_MESSAGE_ID_CLEARDEPTHSTENCILVIEW_MISMATCHINGCLEARVALUE,
                 D3D12_MESSAGE_ID_CLEARRENDERTARGETVIEW_MISMATCHINGCLEARVALUE,
                 D3D12_MESSAGE_ID_CREATEPIPELINELIBRARY_INVALIDLIBRARYBLOB,
+                // Stale data from another driver or adapter is reported as "OUT_OF_DATE"
+                D3D12_MESSAGE_ID_CREATEPIPELINELIBRARY_DRIVERVERSIONMISMATCH,
+                D3D12_MESSAGE_ID_CREATEPIPELINELIBRARY_ADAPTERVERSIONMISMATCH,
+                // A pipeline is looked up in the library before it gets created and stored
+                D3D12_MESSAGE_ID_LOADPIPELINE_NAMENOTFOUND,
 #if NRI_ENABLE_AGILITY_SDK_SUPPORT
                 // Barrier-only command lists are needed for layout transitions around synchronous host copies.
                 // Replacing their synchronization scopes with NONE / NO_ACCESS triggers invalid barrier access validation after a copy.
diff --git a/Source/D3D12/PipelineCacheD3D12.hpp b/Source/D3D12/PipelineCacheD3D12.hpp
index 6a3b9dbf..f6dd53dc 100644
--- a/Source/D3D12/PipelineCacheD3D12.hpp
+++ b/Source/D3D12/PipelineCacheD3D12.hpp
@@ -13,7 +13,20 @@ Result PipelineCacheD3D12::Create(const PipelineCacheDesc& pipelineCacheDesc) {
     HRESULT hr = m_Device->CreatePipelineLibrary(m_Blob.data(), m_Blob.size(), IID_PPV_ARGS(&m_Library));
 
     // If pipeline cache is supported it may fail only on stale/incompatible data, map to "OUT_OF_DATE"
-    return FAILED(hr) ? Result::OUT_OF_DATE : Result::SUCCESS;
+    if (FAILED(hr)) {
+        const char* reason = "not a pipeline library";
+
+        if (hr == D3D12_ERROR_DRIVER_VERSION_MISMATCH)
+            reason = "made by another driver version";
+        else if (hr == D3D12_ERROR_ADAPTER_NOT_FOUND)
+            reason = "made on another adapter";
+
+        NRI_REPORT_INFO(&m_Device, "Pipeline cache data refused: %s (result = 0x%08X)", reason, (uint32_t)hr);
+
+        return Result::OUT_OF_DATE;
+    }
+
+    return Result::SUCCESS;
 }
 
 Result PipelineCacheD3D12::GetData(void* dst, uint64_t& size) const {
